      "id": "rhode-island-holidays",
      "sourceUrl": "https://webserver.rilegislature.gov/Statutes/TITLE25/25-1/25-1-1.htm",
      "title": "The holidays of Rhode Island (R.I. Gen. Laws § 25-1-1) that\n`us-federal-holidays` does not already close: Rhode Island Independence Day\n(May 4, the day after when it falls on a Sunday), Victory Day (the second\nMonday in August), the Monday after a New Year's Day, Juneteenth,\nIndependence Day, Veterans' Day or Christmas Day that falls on a Saturday,\nand election day, the Tuesday after the first Monday in November of each\nyear in which a general election of state officers is held (an even year).\nEach `once` day is listed from the date the vendored text was retrieved\n(October 29, 2026) to the end of 2050. Not modeled: the days the governor,\nthe general assembly, the President or Congress appoints, which no vendored\nsource lists."
    }
